Z||000000||four50four||07-09-99||01:56 PM||||ok up until today i have always thought that they didn't have a getrag (?) 5-speeds until 1987. so far today i have found out from 2 different sources that they came out in 86. also what are the differences between the 4 speed and the 5 speed? i am interested in buying a gt (i like the look) but if i due to lack of funds i am looking for a cheap 5-speed but if the 4-speed is any good than i might go for that one instead. 
Z||000001||Eric||07-09-99||04:22 PM||||I like the 88s, personally, but I've heard good things about the acceleration of the eariler 4 speeds.  The 4 speeds can handle as much power as the 5 speeds, but there is one less gear.  If you don't like to run through the gears, like I do, maybe a 4 speed would be the best thing for you.<p>I wish I had found this forum before I bought my car.  It's a great place to gain information about anything Fiero.  My best advice is not to jump into anything without researching it first.  You are well on your way to owning one of the greatest cars ever made.
Z||000002||lowCG||07-09-99||04:49 PM||||I know of a decent '87,S/E,V6 5spd,power everything for $1500.<br>Ownwers just put $1100 into the brakes,cables...<br>Has the GT nose,engine,trans,and guages,just no 80lb fastback.
