Z||000004||theogre||07-09-99||08:49 PM||||the main thing the 5 speed gives you is better gas milage in 5, since 5 is over driven. 4 in the 4 speed is straight thru I think. maybe a small reduction, but very small.<p>I drove a 84 base 4 speed. 1st geer is so low you are shifting out of it at 10-20mph. Basically the 4 speed is a 3 speed with a mud gear. 1st is so low, and second is low enough, that you can easily pull off a normal, non race, start in second gear. Properly driven a 4 speed will rarely make you shift lower than 3 unless you come to a complete stop.
