Z||000013||Carrolles||07-12-99||11:53 AM||||At 70 mph my 85SE V-6 4spd is turning 3000 rpm while an 87 GT with the 5spd was turning 2200 rpm.  I can get to 60 in 2nd gear in my 4spd (3.63:1 gear set) while the 5spd could get to around 55.<br>The 84 with the high revving engine may have had the 4.10:1 gear set.  Ed Parks has the 4.10 set in his 85 SE V-6 and it is very nice.  At 70 mph it is turning around 3300 rpm which puts it right at the sweet spot of the torque/hp curve and actually gets better mileage at that speed than my 6.63 gears.
